=== srb-P1 (rejection): no WHERE - not a single-row candidate ===
CTE lookup key references a CTE output column that is not part of the virtual primary key.  The virtual CTE primary key matches the CTE body's GROUP BY column list.
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: CTE lookup key references a non-key CTE column.

=== srb-P2 (rejection): WHERE does not touch the PK ===
CTE 'r' has no aggregate functions and no GROUP BY, so it is only supported as a single-row key lookup: its WHERE clause must bind every primary key column of table 'orders' by equality with a constant.  Otherwise add GROUP BY and aggregate functions to the CTE body.
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: Non-aggregating CTE body is not a single-row key lookup.

=== srb-P3 (rejection): PK bound by range, not equality ===
CTE 'r' has no aggregate functions and no GROUP BY, so it is only supported as a single-row key lookup: its WHERE clause must bind every primary key column of table 'orders' by equality with a constant.  Otherwise add GROUP BY and aggregate functions to the CTE body.
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: Non-aggregating CTE body is not a single-row key lookup.

=== srb-P4 (rejection): PK bound to a column-containing expression ===
CTE 'r' has no aggregate functions and no GROUP BY, so it is only supported as a single-row key lookup: its WHERE clause must bind every primary key column of table 'orders' by equality with a constant.  Otherwise add GROUP BY and aggregate functions to the CTE body.
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: Non-aggregating CTE body is not a single-row key lookup.

=== srb-P5 (rejection): expression output in the body ===
Syntax error in SQL statement: Unexpected at this point
> WITH r AS (SELECT o_custkey + 1 AS k FROM orders WHERE o_orderkey = 77) SELECT c.c_custkey FROM customer AS c JOIN r ON r.k = c.c_custkey;
!                             ^
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: Syntax error.

=== srb-P6 (rejection): ORDER BY inside the body still rejected ===
ORDER BY inside CTE body 'r' is not supported. It is only supported at the main SELECT level; accepting it here would silently ignore it, changing results compared to MySQL.
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: ORDER BY / LIMIT in a CTE body or subquery is not supported.

=== srb-P7 (rejection): duplicate output columns ===
CTE 'r' must contain at least one aggregate function.
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: CTE without aggregate function.

=== srb-P8 (rejection): HAVING inside the body ===
CTE 'r' must contain at least one aggregate function.
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: CTE without aggregate function.

=== srb-P9 (rejection): unknown column as a lookup key ===
CTE lookup key references a column that is not an output of the single-row CTE.
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: CTE lookup key references a non-key CTE column.

=== srb-P10 (rejection): no-FROM qualified reference ===
Column qualifier 'r' refers to a single-row CTE.  SELECT without an explicit FROM clause supports only scalar (aggregate-only) CTEs; add an explicit comma cross join instead (FROM t, r).
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: Non-scalar CTE referenced with no FROM clause.

=== srb-P11 (rejection): DATE watermark compare via comma join ===
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: CTE_LOOKUP filter col-vs-col: only integer, FLOAT and DOUBLE operands are supported — DECIMAL, string and temporal comparisons need a cast or a constant-vs-column form.
